{{also|typ|TYP|тур}}
==German==

===Etymology===
{{bor+|de|la|typus||figure, pattern}}, from {{der|de|grc|τύπος||type; impression}}. Compare {{cog|fr|type||guy, bloke}}, and {{cog|es|tipo}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|[tyːp]}}
* {{audio|de|De-Typ.ogg|audio}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|m,s,en}}

# [[type]]
#: {{ux|de|Von diesem '''Typ''' Kaffeemaschine haben wir keine mehr auf Lager.|We don't have any more of this '''type''' of coffeemaker in stock.}}

====Declension====
{{de-ndecl|m,s,en}}

====Related terms====
{{rel4|de
|Prototyp|Stereotyp|Type|typisch|typisieren|Typologie
}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|((<m,s,en>,<m.weak>))|f=in}}

# {{lb|de|colloquial}} [[guy]]; [[bloke]]
#: {{ux|de|Siehst du den komischen '''Typ''' da drüben?|Do you see that strange '''bloke''' over there?}}
#: {{ux|de|Der ist echt ’n toller '''Typ'''!|He’s really a great '''guy'''!}}

====Usage notes====
* In this sense, the noun sometimes has weak singular declension (''des Typen'', etc.), contrarily to the general colloquial tendency to drop weak endings.
* As a female equivalent, {{m|de|Tante||aunt}} is used in a general sense of 'woman'.

